-- title:
--   Probability Theory: cond Entropy of injective
-- statement:
--   If `X : Ω → S`, `Y : Ω → T` are random variables, and `f : T × S → U` is
--     injective for each fixed `t ∈ T`, then `H[f(Y, X) | Y] = H[X | Y]`.
--     Thus for instance `H[X-Y|Y] = H[X|Y]`.
--
--   Source: https://github.com/LeanPool/lean-pool/blob/e110decb9d02249d99fa85a144e6a659dea91440/LeanPool/ZhangYeungInequality/PFR/ForMathlib/Entropy/Basic.lean#L551-L567
